# A batch file is read by cmd.exe, which is happier with CRLF and, for `goto`
# in particular, has historically needed it. Git's autocrlf setting is a local
# preference and cannot be relied on, so the line endings are pinned here
# instead — for the file and for the checkout, on every platform.
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# The launcher shipped on Linux and macOS is read by /bin/sh, which treats a
# trailing CR as part of the last word on the line. A checkout with autocrlf
# on would produce a script that fails with "bad interpreter".
*.sh text eol=lf
